      "math_academy_id": "q-182514",
      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬(¬P∧Q)\\,$ | $\\,P∨¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-2}} | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n\n \n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\n¬(¬P∧Q){{field-4}}P∨¬Q\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∨¬Q & ≡\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{F}$ and $Q≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(¬P∧Q) & ≡¬(¬\\text{F}∧\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡¬(\\text{T}∧\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{F}$ and $Q≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∨¬Q & ≡\\text{F}∨¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬(¬P∧Q)\\,$ | $\\,P∨¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $¬(¬P∧Q)$ is logically equivalent to $P∨¬Q,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{T},\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{T}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n¬(¬P∧Q)≡P∨¬Q.\n$$",
